---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Mobile concepts — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"Independent music production and creative audio publication."}
  canonicalPath={"/internal/mobile-matrix/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={true}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .sheet-note { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .sheet-note h1 { max-width: 18ch; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .sheet-note .lede { margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 60ch; }

  .frames {
    display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    justify-content: start;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 390px), 390px));
  }

  /* A browser shell, not a phone shell: this is one responsive web product
     at a 390px viewport, not a native app. */
  .frame { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; }
  .frame__chrome {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-media);
  }
  /* The iframe is pinned to a true 390px viewport, so on a narrower screen
     the shell scrolls internally rather than the page scrolling sideways —
     the measurement stays honest either way. */
  @media (max-width: 460px) { .frame__chrome { overflow-x: auto; } }
  .frame__bar {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.625rem;
    padding: 0.625rem 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 4%, var(--surface));
  }
  .frame__dots { display: flex; gap: 5px; flex: none; }
  .frame__dots i { inline-size: 8px; block-size: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--line-strong); }
  .frame__url {
    flex: 1; min-width: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--muted); background: var(--canvas);
    padding: 0.3125rem 0.625rem; border-radius: 6px;
    white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .frame iframe { display: block; width: 390px; height: 760px; border: 0; background: var(--canvas); }
  .frame__cap {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .frame__cap strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 550; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }

  .checks { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .checks li {
    padding-block: 0.875rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .checks li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .checks li::before {
    content: ""; inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--status-ok); margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">
  <section class="sheet-note">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="kicker">Concept — mobile</p>
      <h1>The same pages at 390 px</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These are the live concept pages rendered at a 390 px viewport, not separate
        mobile mock-ups. The shell is a browser rather than a phone on purpose: this is
        one responsive web publication, not a native app.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell">
    <div class="frames">

      <figure class="frame">
        <div class="frame__chrome" tabindex="0" aria-label="Horizontal scrollbare Mobilvorschau">
          <div class="frame__bar">
            <span class="frame__dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="frame__url">auspiciousmusic.com</span>
          </div>
          <iframe src="/" title="Homepage at 390 pixels wide" loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="frame__cap">
          <strong>Homepage</strong>
          Brand, menu, H1, supporting copy, primary action and the top of the artwork
          all land in the first viewport without clipping.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="frame">
        <div class="frame__chrome" tabindex="0" aria-label="Horizontal scrollbare Mobilvorschau">
          <div class="frame__bar">
            <span class="frame__dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="frame__url">auspiciousmusic.com/#menu</span>
          </div>
          <iframe src="/#menu" title="Full-screen menu at 390 pixels wide" loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="frame__cap">
          <strong>Menu</strong>
          Full-screen sheet, seven destinations at display size, no nested accordion.
          Escape and the close control both dismiss it.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="frame">
        <div class="frame__chrome" tabindex="0" aria-label="Horizontal scrollbare Mobilvorschau">
          <div class="frame__bar">
            <span class="frame__dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="frame__url">auspiciousmusic.com/sound-design/…</span>
          </div>
          <iframe src="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/" title="Long-form article at 390 pixels wide" loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="frame__cap">
          <strong>Long-form article</strong>
          Contents collapse to an inline disclosure, the requirements table reflows to
          two columns, and the settings block scrolls horizontally rather than shrinking.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band band--tight band-surface">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 style="font-size:var(--t-h3);margin-bottom:1.5rem">What was re-composed rather than stacked</h2>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li>Navigation becomes a full-screen sheet with display-scale type, not a shrunken bar.</li>
        <li>The masthead keeps its full-viewport height, but the headline centres in the free row instead of sitting at the bottom — bottom-weighting left a dead field above it on a short screen.</li>
        <li>The string drops to the baseline of the headline. Running through the middle of a short word, a full-width line reads as a strikethrough rather than a string.</li>
        <li>The two hero actions go full width and stack below 400px, rather than sitting as two half-width buttons on one cramped row.</li>
        <li>Topic portals lose their four-column rail and become title-first blocks with the description underneath.</li>
        <li>The editorial index drops its date and topic columns into the row body, keeping one tap target per article.</li>
        <li>Article contents collapse from a sticky side rail into an inline disclosure at the top of the piece.</li>
        <li>The settings block and the calculator tables keep their monospace alignment and scroll sideways instead of reflowing into nonsense — and the caption says so, because a table that scrolls silently reads as a table with missing columns.</li>
        <li>Legacy fact tables and article metadata switch from two columns to stacked label-and-value pairs below 560px.</li>
        <li>Form fields are lifted to 16px on touch, because anything smaller makes iOS zoom the viewport on focus and leave the page scrolled sideways.</li>
        <li>Row highlights move from <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.9em">:hover</span> to <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.9em">:active</span> where there is no pointer, so a tapped row does not stay highlighted after you have moved on.</li>
        <li>The gutter becomes a floor against the display cutout, and the menu sheet and footer clear the home indicator.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>